 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186458824 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459184 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186458898 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459184 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186458930 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459184 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186459049 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459184 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459184 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459184 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186458898 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459184 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "d8314db3-fd94-5934-8c57-06ecde0d8fcc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459193 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186458626 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459193 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186458802 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459193 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186458908 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459193 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186458984 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459193 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186459071 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459193 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459193 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459193 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186458626 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459193 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "e99b453b-e56a-5891-a94b-5ab07ced0185" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459214 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186459125 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459214 #edb/ref 1069 "q-98163" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459214 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459214 #edb/ref 1071 "Calculate ${\\int }_{0}^{1}[\\frac{2}{3}f(t)+\\frac{1}{2}g(t)]\\,\\text{d}t$ given that ${\\int }_{0}^{1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨3,\\,6,\\,-3⟩$ and ${\\int }_{0}^{1}g(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨4,\\,2,\\,10⟩.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459214 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "1b76a888-c386-580d-abe0-7db8002d6871" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459214 #edb/ref 1074 "From the vector addition and scalar multiplication rules, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{1}[\\frac{2}{3}f(t)+\\frac{1}{2}g(t)]\\,\\text{d}t=\\frac{2}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t+\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}g(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}[\\frac{2}{3}f(t)+\\frac{1}{2}g(t)]\\,\\text{d}t & =\\frac{2}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t+\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}g(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}⟨3,\\,6,\\,-3⟩+\\frac{1}{2}⟨4,\\,2,\\,10⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,\\,4,\\,-2⟩+⟨2,\\,1,\\,5⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4,\\,5,\\,3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459224 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186459089 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459224 #edb/ref 1069 "q-129274" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459224 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459224 #edb/ref 1071 "Calculate \n${\\int }_{2}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t$\ngiven that\n${\\int }_{2}^{0}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨-4,\\,-6,\\,4⟩$\nand\n${\\int }_{0}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨9,\\,9,\\,-6⟩.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459224 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "32ebf6aa-8547-5777-9834-260892a9ca32" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459224 #edb/ref 1074 "Using the adjacent intervals rule, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t={\\int }_{0}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{2}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the above as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{2}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t={\\int }_{0}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t-{\\int }_{0}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nFinally, using the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{2}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t-(-{\\int }_{2}^{0}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t) \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{2}^{0}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =⟨9,\\,9,\\,-6⟩+⟨-4,\\,-6,\\,4⟩ \\\\  & =⟨5,\\,3,\\,-2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459225 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186459167 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459225 #edb/ref 1069 "q-129290" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459225 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459225 #edb/ref 1071 "Find ${\\int }_{1}^{2}c\\cdot f(t)\\,\\text{d}t$ \ngiven that \n${\\int }_{1}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\,i+\\,j+2\\pi \\,k$ \nand \n$c=2\\,i-\\,k.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459225 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "3643194d-d38f-5e28-b2ac-1e1d3a327966" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459225 #edb/ref 1074 "The dot product rule states that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1}^{2}c\\cdot f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=c\\cdot {\\int }_{1}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nApplying the dot-product rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}c\\cdot f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =c\\cdot {\\int }_{1}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =(2\\,i-\\,k)\\cdot (\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\,i+\\,j+2\\pi \\,k) \\\\  & =\\pi -2\\pi  \\\\  & =-\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459237 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186459090 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459237 #edb/ref 1069 "q-129152" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459237 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459237 #edb/ref 1071 "Calculate ${\\int }_{1}^{3}[4f(t)-3g(t)]\\,\\text{d}t$ given that ${\\int }_{1}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨-\\frac{1}{4},\\,-\\frac{3}{2},\\,-2⟩$ and ${\\int }_{1}^{3}g(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨\\frac{2}{3},\\,-1,\\,2⟩.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459237 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "502c15a4-2b20-54ef-9a03-875448a388c3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459237 #edb/ref 1074 "From the vector addition and scalar multiplication rules, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1}^{3}[4f(t)-3g(t)]\\,\\text{d}t=4{\\int }_{1}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t-3{\\int }_{1}^{3}g(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{3}[4f(t)-3g(t)]\\,\\text{d}t & =4{\\int }_{1}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t-3{\\int }_{1}^{3}g(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =4⟨-\\frac{1}{4},\\,-\\frac{3}{2},\\,-2⟩-3⟨\\frac{2}{3},\\,-1,\\,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,\\,-6,\\,-8⟩-⟨2,\\,-3,\\,6⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-3,\\,-3,\\,-14⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459243 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186459108 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459243 #edb/ref 1069 "q-98214" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459243 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459243 #edb/ref 1071 "Calculate \n${\\int }_{1}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t$\ngiven that\n${\\int }_{1}^{5}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨4,\\,2,\\,-3⟩$\nand\n${\\int }_{5}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨-1,\\,2,\\,-7⟩.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459243 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "626ec44a-73a5-5e9b-9066-3e6a39d1e10e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459243 #edb/ref 1074 "Using the adjacent intervals rule, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1}^{5}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t={\\int }_{1}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{3}^{5}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the above as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t={\\int }_{1}^{5}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t-{\\int }_{3}^{5}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nFinally, using the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{1}^{5}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t-{\\int }_{3}^{5}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{5}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{5}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =⟨4,\\,2,\\,-3⟩+⟨-1,\\,2,\\,-7⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,\\,4,\\,-10⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459246 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186459163 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459246 #edb/ref 1069 "q-129153" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459246 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459246 #edb/ref 1071 "Calculate ${\\int }_{0}^{1}[f(t)+2g(t)]\\,\\text{d}t$ given that ${\\int }_{0}^{1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨-3,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡1,\\,-1⟩$ and ${\\int }_{0}^{1}g(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨5,\\,1,\\,-2⟩.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459246 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "6b5a16e8-c13d-51bd-9dfe-f5d38efff2fe" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459246 #edb/ref 1074 "From the vector addition and scalar multiplication rules, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{1}[f(t)+2g(t)]\\,\\text{d}t={\\int }_{0}^{1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t+2{\\int }_{0}^{1}g(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}[f(t)+2g(t)]\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t+2{\\int }_{0}^{1}g(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =⟨-3,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡1,\\,-1⟩+2⟨5,\\,1,\\,-2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-3,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡1,\\,-1⟩+⟨10,\\,2,\\,-4⟩ \\\\  & =⟨7,\\,2+\\operatorname{sin}⁡1,\\,-5⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459249 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186459086 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459249 #edb/ref 1069 "q-129138" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459249 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459249 #edb/ref 1071 "Calculate \n${\\int }_{-1}^{3}[\\frac{1}{3}f(t)+2g(t)]\\text{d}t$ \ngiven that \n${\\int }_{-1}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨-3,\\,6,\\,3⟩$\nand \n${\\int }_{-1}^{3}g(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨-\\frac{1}{2},\\,1,\\,-1⟩.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459249 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "7358da91-8014-5776-8731-ceb0c31740d0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459249 #edb/ref 1074 "From the vector addition and scalar multiplication rules, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-1}^{3}[\\frac{1}{3}f(t)+2g(t)]\\text{d}t=\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{-1}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t+2{\\int }_{-1}^{3}g(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{3}[\\frac{1}{3}f(t)+2g(t)]\\,\\text{d}t & =\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{-1}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t+2{\\int }_{-1}^{3}g(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}⟨-3,\\,6,\\,3⟩+2⟨-\\frac{1}{2},\\,1,\\,-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,\\,2,\\,1⟩+⟨-1,\\,2,\\,-2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2,\\,4,\\,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459254 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186459193 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459254 #edb/ref 1069 "q-98175" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459254 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459254 #edb/ref 1071 "Calculate \n${\\int }_{1}^{0}2f(t)\\,\\text{d}t$\ngiven that\n${\\int }_{0}^{1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨e-1,\\,1,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡1⟩.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459254 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "7c945750-33b2-55ee-8335-b093fb35e399" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459254 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's reverse the limits of integration on the known result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{0}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =-{\\int }_{0}^{1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-⟨e-1,\\,1,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1-e,\\,-1,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, applying the scalar multiplication rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{0}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =2{\\int }_{1}^{0}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =2\\cdot ⟨1-e,\\,-1,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2-2e,\\,-2,\\,-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459259 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186459175 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459259 #edb/ref 1069 "q-98215" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459259 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459259 #edb/ref 1071 "Calculate \n${\\int }_{4}^{5}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t$\ngiven that\n${\\int }_{4}^{7}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨3,\\,-5,\\,-6⟩$\nand\n${\\int }_{5}^{7}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨-2,\\,-9,\\,8⟩.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459259 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "8f6b1824-8799-5b59-8e80-5a3b112af87a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459259 #edb/ref 1074 "Using the adjacent intervals rule, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{4}^{7}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t={\\int }_{4}^{5}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{5}^{7}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the above as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{4}^{5}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t={\\int }_{4}^{7}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t-{\\int }_{5}^{7}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nFinally, using the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{4}^{5}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{4}^{7}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t-{\\int }_{5}^{7}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =⟨3,\\,-5,\\,-6⟩-⟨-2,\\,-9,\\,8⟩ \\\\  & =⟨5,\\,4,\\,-14⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459262 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186459178 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459262 #edb/ref 1069 "q-129181" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459262 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459262 #edb/ref 1071 "Calculate \n${\\int }_{2}^{0}5f(t)\\,\\text{d}t$\ngiven that\n${\\int }_{0}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨-e,\\,{e}^{2},\\,-1⟩.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459262 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "94efa4a2-1092-5b11-ab4d-7217c29637ba" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459262 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's reverse the limits of integration on the known result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{2}^{0}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =-{\\int }_{0}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-⟨-e,\\,{e}^{2},\\,-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨e,\\,-{e}^{2},\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, applying the scalar multiplication rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{2}^{0}5f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =5{\\int }_{2}^{0}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =5\\cdot ⟨e,\\,-{e}^{2},\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨5e,\\,-5{e}^{2},\\,5⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459290 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186459161 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459290 #edb/ref 1069 "q-129267" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459290 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459290 #edb/ref 1071 "Calculate \n${\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{3}{2}f(t)+⟨2,\\,-1,\\,-2⟩\\,\\text{d}t$\ngiven that\n${\\int }_{2}^{0}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨10,\\,4,\\,-2⟩.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459290 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d15da025-4086-5540-bf68-ef7b03d66ed0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459290 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's reverse the limits of integration on the known result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =-{\\int }_{2}^{0}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-⟨10,\\,4,\\,-2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-10,\\,-4,\\,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, applying the vector addition rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{3}{2}f(t)+⟨2,\\,-1,\\,-2⟩\\,\\text{d}t & =\\frac{3}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{0}^{2}⟨2,\\,-1,\\,-2⟩\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}⟨-10,\\,-4,\\,2⟩+⟨2t,\\,-t,\\,-2t⟩{|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =⟨-15,\\,-6,\\,3⟩+⟨4,\\,-2,\\,-4⟩\\text{ } \\\\  & =⟨-11,\\,-8,\\,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459297 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186459174 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459297 #edb/ref 1069 "q-32519" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459297 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459297 #edb/ref 1071 "Calculate ${\\int }_{0}^{1}[f(t)-g(t)]\\,\\text{d}t$ given that ${\\int }_{0}^{1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨\\frac{1}{2},\\,2,\\,1⟩$ and ${\\int }_{0}^{1}g(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨1,\\,1,\\,1⟩.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459297 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e1a63430-5da8-52e4-a931-6317cfed822f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459297 #edb/ref 1074 "From the vector addition rule, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{1}[f(t)-g(t)]\\,\\text{d}t={\\int }_{0}^{1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t-{\\int }_{0}^{1}g(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}[f(t)-g(t)]\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t-{\\int }_{0}^{1}g(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1}{2},\\,2,\\,1⟩-⟨1,\\,1,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{1}{2},\\,1,\\,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459307 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186459184 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459307 #edb/ref 1069 "q-32497" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459307 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459307 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that \n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=2\\pi \\,i+\\pi \\,j+(2-\\pi )\\,k,$ \n$c=i+u\\,j,$\nand \n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }c\\cdot f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=0,$ what is the value of $u?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459307 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "fa2f9f9d-09dc-55fa-a8fa-ab5f37e6b68d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459307 #edb/ref 1074 "The dot product rule states that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }c\\cdot f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=c\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nApplying the dot-product rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }c\\cdot f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =c\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =(i+u\\,j)\\cdot (2\\pi \\,i+\\pi \\,j+(2-\\pi )\\,k) \\\\  & =2\\pi +u\\cdot \\pi +0\\cdot (2-\\pi ) \\\\  & =\\pi (2+u).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since ${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }c\\cdot f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=0,$ we must have $\\pi (2+u)=0,$ which means that $u=-2.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
